# Settings and Persistence Architecture

## Overview
Juno implements a comprehensive settings system with persistent storage, real-time updates, and type-safe frontend integration. Settings are managed through a combination of Tauri commands, tauri-plugin-store, and React hooks.

## Backend Persistence

### Storage Technology
- **Primary**: [tauri-plugin-store](mdc:https:/github.com/tauri-apps/plugins-workspace/tree/v2/plugins/store) - Tauri's official persistent storage
- **Format**: JSON files in application data directory
- **Structure**: Multiple store files for different setting categories

### Store Files
- `"agent_settings.json"` - Agent-specific settings (trigger mode, etc.)
- `"user_settings.json"` - General user preferences
- Additional specialized stores as needed

### Storage Implementation Pattern
Located in [src-tauri/src/commands/core.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/commands/core.rs):
```rust
use tauri_plugin_store::{Store, StoreExt};

#[tauri::command]
async fn set_agent_trigger_mode(
    app: tauri::AppHandle,
    mode: AgentTriggerMode,
) -> Result<(), String> {
    // Get or create store
    let mut store = app.store_builder("agent_settings.json").build()?;

    // Save setting
    store.set("agent_trigger_mode", mode.clone())?;
    store.save()?;

    // Update runtime state
    app.state::<AppState>().set_agent_trigger_mode(mode);
    Ok(())
}
```

## Frontend Settings Management

### Settings Hook
Centralized settings management in [src/hooks/useSettings.ts](mdc:src/hooks/useSettings.ts):
```typescript
export const useSettings = () => {
  const [agentTriggerMode, setAgentTriggerMode] = useState<AgentTriggerMode>('Tap');

  // Load settings on mount
  useEffect(() => {
    loadSettings();
  }, []);

  // Setting change handlers
  const handleAgentTriggerModeChange = async (mode: AgentTriggerMode) => {
    await invoke('set_agent_trigger_mode', { mode });
    setAgentTriggerMode(mode);
  };

  return {
    agentTriggerMode,
    handleAgentTriggerModeChange,
    // ... other settings
  };
};
```

