## State Synchronization

### Runtime State Management
Primary state container in [src-tauri/src/state.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/state.rs):
```rust
pub struct AppState {
    // Settings cached in memory for performance
    agent_trigger_mode: Arc<Mutex<AgentTriggerMode>>,
    // ... other cached settings
}

impl AppState {
    pub fn set_agent_trigger_mode(&self, mode: AgentTriggerMode) {
        *self.agent_trigger_mode.lock().unwrap() = mode;
    }

    pub fn get_agent_trigger_mode(&self) -> AgentTriggerMode {
        self.agent_trigger_mode.lock().unwrap().clone()
    }
}
```

### Initialization Pattern
Settings loaded on app startup in [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs):
```rust
// Load persistent settings into runtime state
if let Ok(mode) = load_agent_trigger_mode_from_store(&app).await {
    app.state::<AppState>().set_agent_trigger_mode(mode);
}
```

## Implementation Patterns

### Adding New Settings

#### 1. Backend Implementation
```rust
// 1. Add to state.rs
pub struct AppState {
    new_setting: Arc<Mutex<NewSettingType>>,
}

// 2. Add getter/setter methods
impl AppState {
    pub fn get_new_setting(&self) -> NewSettingType { /* ... */ }
    pub fn set_new_setting(&self, value: NewSettingType) { /* ... */ }
}

// 3. Add Tauri commands in commands/core.rs
#[tauri::command]
async fn get_new_setting(app: tauri::AppHandle) -> Result<NewSettingType, String> {
    // Load from store or return default
}

#[tauri::command]
async fn set_new_setting(
    app: tauri::AppHandle,
    value: NewSettingType
) -> Result<(), String> {
    // Save to store and update state
}
```

#### 2. Frontend Integration
```typescript
// 1. Add to useSettings hook
const [newSetting, setNewSetting] = useState<NewSettingType>(defaultValue);

const handleNewSettingChange = async (value: NewSettingType) => {
  await invoke('set_new_setting', { value });
  setNewSetting(value);
};

// 2. Add UI in appropriate settings section
<SettingControl
  value={newSetting}
  onChange={handleNewSettingChange}
  // ... other props
/>
```

### Error Handling
```rust
// Backend error handling
#[tauri::command]
async fn set_setting(app: tauri::AppHandle, value: String) -> Result<(), String> {
    match app.store_builder("settings.json").build() {
        Ok(mut store) => {
            store.set("key", value)?;
            store.save().map_err(|e| e.to_string())
        }
        Err(e) => Err(format!("Store error: {}", e))
    }
}
```

```typescript
// Frontend error handling
const handleSettingChange = async (value: string) => {
  try {
    await invoke('set_setting', { value });
    setSetting(value);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to save setting:', error);
    // Show user notification
  }
};
```

