## Performance Considerations

### Caching Strategy
- Settings loaded once on startup into runtime state
- Immediate access via AppState getters (no async calls)
- Persistence happens asynchronously in background
- Frontend state synchronized with backend changes

### Batch Updates
For multiple related settings:
```rust
#[tauri::command]
async fn update_multiple_settings(
    app: tauri::AppHandle,
    settings: HashMap<String, serde_json::Value>
) -> Result<(), String> {
    let mut store = app.store_builder("settings.json").build()?;

    for (key, value) in settings {
        store.set(key, value)?;
    }

    store.save()?;
    // Update runtime state
    Ok(())
}
```

## Migration and Versioning

### Schema Evolution
```rust
// Handle setting migrations
async fn migrate_settings(app: &tauri::AppHandle) -> Result<(), String> {
    let store = app.store_builder("settings.json").build()?;

    // Check version and migrate if needed
    if let Some(version) = store.get("schema_version") {
        match version.as_u64() {
            Some(1) => migrate_from_v1(&store)?,
            Some(2) => migrate_from_v2(&store)?,
            _ => {}, // Current version
        }
    }

    Ok(())
}
```

